    "path": "$.structures[0].microstructure_list[3]",
    "reason": "Block b0164 reports that in this Fe-3.5Mn-5.8Al-0.35C steel, after fast cooling to 500–600 °C and isothermal annealing for 60 min, the final microstructure consists of a polygonal ferritic matrix and lamellae along prior γ grain boundaries containing fine α-ferrite, κ-carbide and retained austenite (γR), with the γ phase partially decomposed by a eutectoid reaction γ→κ+α+γR; the γR/κ boundaries are coherent. (Condition noted as an isothermal/anustempering-type heat treatment of the same alloy.)",
